  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gender programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">These are spelt out in more detail under the six different projects in the Gender Programme structure below. In summary they are: 
&quot;	to raise and deepen awareness of issues of gender-based violence among church communities as well as other social groupings.
&quot;	to develop a better understanding of how men&apos;s attitudes, beliefs and  understanding of their identity contributes to gender inequalities.
&quot;	to facilitate women&apos;s theological and spiritual development: to contribute to a gendered understanding of poverty and how women cope and survive in a rural or semi-rural setting given the HIV/AIDS situation.
&quot;	to research and develop an intervention in the HIV/AIDS crisis that targets the most vulnerable at the most impressionable stage of their lives - i.e. pre-teen and teenage children.
&quot;	to generate a vision of hope with respect to HIV/AIDS in the churches and in society as a whole.</narrative>
  </description>
